\p{Here is then Rónyai’s theorem.}

\transclude{CC1X}

\p{Note another way of arriving at a contradiction. The set}

##{\bigg\lbrace  \prod_{i \in I} X_i : I \subset [m] \bigg\rbrace}

\p{of #{2^m} monomials is a basis for the vector space of functions #{\lbrace 0, 1\rbrace ^m \to \mathbb{Z}_p} over #{\mathbb{Z}_p}, but the coefficient #{c_{[m]}} in the expansion of #{h(X)} above is nonzero, in fact, #{c_{[m]} = 2 \neq 0 \in \mathbb{Z}_p}.}
